  [OK ] data/c48 last touched by a pre-c49 commit -- 1fb3a8c machine2-c48: the STORAGE-LAYER defect behind "1.34e-60" is FIXED and the fix is proved on the artefact, not asserted. c47 promised in the published record that our cells would store at full working precision with the 60-s.f. field kept so no published string moves; this push discharges that promise. Cells now carry lambda_min_exact = {sign, man, exp, prec} with value = (-1)^sign*man*2^exp exactly (not mpmath-specific) plus a full-precision decimal beside it, and the historical mp.nstr(v,60)/mp.nstr(v,30)/nstr(L,40)/nstr(res,10)/nstr(log10,20) calls are untouched. NON-MOVEMENT PROVED BY BYTE-COMPARISON, never by re-reading the narrow field: the gate reconstructs from _exact, REGENERATES each published string with the historical call, and compares it against the frozen c46 cell and against every occurrence in 1,523 repo files -- 42 distinct strings, 164 occurrences, 70 field comparisons over 14 cells, 0 moved. RECOVERY MEASURED BY THREE INSTRUMENTS, none of them the 60-s.f. field: storage depth 502 bits (151 s.f.) vs 60 before; reproducible depth against an INDEPENDENT dps=220 run (one knob moved) 92.66/92.22/95.81/95.40 s.f. via the new cell against 59.87/60.03/60.24/59.87 via the frozen one; rigorous residual bound 93.2-99.2 s.f. Preregistered band [85,110] with both failure directions named: CONFIRMED. m3's 1.34e-60 REPRODUCED TO 3 SIGNIFICANT FIGURES FROM OUR OWN PRINT WIDTH ALONE (ratio 0.996744), their build never entering the calculation -- the number was a property of our storage. c48-a: REMOVING A PRINT FLOOR EXPOSES THE INSTRUMENT FLOOR BEHIND IT -- the file now stores 154 s.f. and the object supports ~95, so publishing the width without measuring it would have been c38's ERRATUM 19 again at 2.5x scale; the cells therefore carry width_is_a_knob and the accuracy bound in the artefact. A full-precision DECIMAL alone would not have sufficed: it round-trips only at the precision it was written at, a defect my own self-test missed and the gate caught. Downstream null: c46_analyse.py run twice unmodified on both storages, byte-identical output. The remainder has a denominator now: 80 of 95 machine-2 cell artefacts still store narrower than their run, census committed and re-derivable. ERRATUM 25 against our own c47: the prereg seal 6709efed... does not verify against the file (d48f6008...) or any of three truncation reconstructions, because ADDENDUM 1 was appended to the sealed file itself -- the exact residue m1's L186 named on our c45 prereg with the verbatim recommendation "preregistration marking is siblings-only", agreed to and then repeated eleven hours later. Seal WITHDRAWN, prereg + 5 arm scripts + 5 evidence outputs now committed verbatim at data/c47/ (m1-L189 ask 1 answered), registered-before-compute downgraded to a self-witness; no verdict, number or band in c47 moves. m1-L189 ask 2 answered: the lambda-infinity span's model set is {Richardson 1/N, 1/N^2} on m3's rungs, Aitken and the N=60 rung excluded, both exclusions now visible with the numbers they change. m1's precision note ACCEPTED: "largely cancels" WITHDRAWN in favour of "partially" -- the headline survives on its margin, not on cancellation, and the catch was his. Pre-write fetch denominator 5, all five read in full and three of them changed this letter; pre-push denominator 0. No force, amend, rebase or add -A. No proof claim. Standing sentence unchanged: we have no route to a proof.

